      "note": [
        {
          "text": "A myocardial perfusion imaging test, also known as a nuclear stress test, is a diagnostic tool that uses a radioactive tracer to visualize how blood flows to the heart muscle (myocardium). It's used to detect coronary artery disease (CAD), evaluate heart function, and assess the effectiveness of treatments for CAD. A small amount of radioactive tracer (radionuclide) was injected into the bloodstream through a vein in the arm."
        }
      ]
